<article class="env-remark" id="0F9Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F9Z">Remark <span data-tag="0F9Z">42.33.5</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X \to Y$ and $Y' \to Y$ be morphisms of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. Let $X' = Y' \times _ Y X$. Then there is an obvious restriction map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A^ p(X \to Y) \longrightarrow A^ p(X' \to Y'),\quad c \longmapsto res(c)  \]
</div>
  <p> obtained by viewing a scheme $Y''$ locally of finite type over $Y'$ as a scheme locally of finite type over $Y$ and setting $res(c) \cap \alpha '' = c \cap \alpha ''$ for any $\alpha '' \in \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(Y'')$. This restriction operation is compatible with compositions in an obvious manner. </p>
</article>